  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nA upper-level low is expected to track across the Texas Panhandle\nand lift to the Kansas/Oklahoma border, with an associated \nsurface cold front tracking southeast across our area Monday \nnight. There are some rain chances in the forecast, but the remain\nprimarily dependent on the track of the aforementioned system and\nhaving enough lift to produce showers. At this time, appears that\nthere will be enough lift, moisture and instability for a band of\nshowers and thunderstorms to develop along the cold front, as it \npushes across our area. The higher rain chances and better \ncoverage of convection look to be in our eastern and southeastern \ncounties where more moisture should be available. At this time,  \nSPC has our area outlooked in a Marginal Risk for severe\nthunderstorms for Monday. \n\nCooler air will follow this cold front on Monday, and will be \naccompanied by breezy north to northwest winds on Tuesday. Monday\nwill see high temperatures in the upper 70s to mid 80s, but highs\non Tuesday behind the front will struggle to surpass the lower to\nmid 70s. Dry weather to follow for Wednesday though Friday, as \nsurface high pressure settles into Texas.",
